  "task": {
    "objective": "Build and provision sixteen settlements while maintaining renewable woodland, crops, water and safe shared routes; trade local production against transport access and neighboring ecological costs.",
    "natural_termination": "No early natural success/failure threshold. Persistent world changes continue until the896-turn season truncates. Incapacitated actors retain wait and can receive aid; terminal raw calls absorb.",
    "interaction": "Cutting mature trees opens pack routes but changes delayed regrowth, local well recharge and fire exposure. Loaded NPC pack animals traverse shared trails and bridges. Equipment exchange, carried goods, shared aquifer flow, rescue, village upgrades and finite trade commissions create partner-dependent choices.",
    "observation_access": "Static terrain is public. Dynamic groups use Manhattan radius5, distance then id order, with8 settlers,12 tree sites and3 per other group. Every visible scene attribute is in native observations; hidden slots are zero. Fire reports are locally posted information from a neighboring village and age over time."
  },
